# Canvas Design

## Overview

Create 2D graphics using HTML5 Canvas API.

## Basics

### Setup
```html
<canvas id="myCanvas" width="800" height="600"></canvas>
<script>
  const canvas = document.getElementById('myCanvas');
  const ctx = canvas.getContext('2d');
</script>
```

### Drawing Shapes

```javascript
// Rectangle
ctx.fillStyle = 'blue';
ctx.fillRect(x, y, width, height);

// Circle
ctx.beginPath();
ctx.arc(x, y, radius, 0, Math.PI * 2);
ctx.fillStyle = 'red';
ctx.fill();

// Line
ctx.beginPath();
ctx.moveTo(x1, y1);
ctx.lineTo(x2, y2);
ctx.stroke();
```

### Paths

```javascript
ctx.beginPath();
ctx.moveTo(0, 0);
ctx.lineTo(100, 100);
ctx.lineTo(100, 0);
ctx.closePath();
ctx.stroke();
```

## Transformations

```javascript
ctx.translate(x, y);    // Move origin
ctx.rotate(angle);      // Rotate
ctx.scale(x, y);        // Scale
ctx.save();             // Save state
ctx.restore();          // Restore state
```

## Text

```javascript
ctx.font = '24px Arial';
ctx.fillStyle = 'black';
ctx.fillText('Hello', x, y);
```

## Images

```javascript
const img = new Image();
img.onload = () => {
  ctx.drawImage(img, x, y, width, height);
};
img.src = 'path/to/image.png';
```

## Animation

```javascript
function animate() {
  ctx.clearRect(0, 0, canvas.width, canvas.height);
  // Draw frame
  requestAnimationFrame(animate);
}
```

---

## Best Practices

1. Use requestAnimationFrame for smooth animations
2. Clear canvas before each frame
3. Save/restore state when using transformations
4. Consider device pixel ratio for crisp rendering
5. Use paths for complex shapes

